# GAgent Integration Testing Guide for Aevatar GAgents

## Overview
This guide provides comprehensive patterns and best practices for writing integration tests for GAgents in the Aevatar framework. Integration tests validate the complete system behavior including Orleans silo, in-memory databases, multi-agent communication, and end-to-end workflows. Each test project should define its own TestBase and TestModule following the patterns established in this guide.

## Part 1: Integration Test Infrastructure Setup

### CRITICAL: Orleans Silo and Cluster Setup
Integration tests require a fully functional Orleans cluster with silo, storage providers, and all necessary services. **DO NOT** implement `ISiloConfigurator` in individual test projects. All Orleans-related service injection should be handled through the `ClusterFixture` in the `Aevatar.GAgents.TestBase` project.

#### Orleans Cluster Infrastructure
The `ClusterFixture` handles:
- **Orleans Silo Startup**: Complete silo configuration with all required services
- **In-Memory Storage**: MongoDB in-memory providers for state persistence
- **Event Sourcing**: Orleans event store configuration
- **Service Registration**: All GAgent dependencies and factories
- **Cluster Communication**: Multi-silo coordination (if needed)

If you need to register additional services for Orleans Grains/GAgents to use, add them to the `TestSiloConfigurations.Configure` method in `ClusterFixture.cs`.

### 1.1 Integration Test Module Definition
Each integration test project should define its own test module inheriting from `AbpModule` with full infrastructure setup:

```csharp
using Aevatar.GAgents.TestBase;
using Volo.Abp.Modularity;

namespace Aevatar.GAgents.YourModule.Test;

[DependsOn(
    typeof(AevatarGAgentTestBaseModule),
    typeof(AevatarGAgentsYourModule) // The module being tested
)]
public class AevatarYourModuleTestModule : AbpModule
{
    public override void ConfigureServices(ServiceConfigurationContext context)
    {
        var services = context.Services;
        
        // Integration test specific configurations
        // Note: Orleans cluster and MongoDB are handled by AevatarGAgentTestBaseModule
        
        // Configure external service clients for integration testing
        services.AddHttpClient();
        
        // Configure test-specific storage providers if needed
        // (MongoDB in-memory is already configured in base module)
        
        // Register any additional test infrastructure services
        services.AddSingleton<ITestDataSeeder, YourModuleTestDataSeeder>();
        
        // Configure logging for integration tests
        services.Configure<AbpLoggerOptions>(options =>
        {
            options.LogLevel = LogLevel.Debug; // More verbose for integration tests
        });
    }
}
```

### 1.2 Integration Test Base Class
Each integration test project should define its own test base class with infrastructure access:

```csharp
using Aevatar.GAgents.TestBase;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Orleans;
using Aevatar.Core.Abstractions;

namespace Aevatar.GAgents.YourModule.Test;

public abstract class AevatarYourModuleTestBase : AevatarGAgentTestBase<AevatarYourModuleTestModule>
{
    protected readonly IGAgentFactory GAgentFactory;
    protected readonly IClusterClient ClusterClient;
    
    protected AevatarYourModuleTestBase()
    {
        GAgentFactory = GetRequiredService<IGAgentFactory>();
        ClusterClient = GetRequiredService<IClusterClient>();
    }
    
    /// <summary>
    /// Setup complex multi-agent system for integration testing
    /// </summary>
    protected async Task<IntegrationTestSystem> SetupTestSystemAsync()
    {
        // Create coordinator and worker agents
        var coordinator = await GAgentFactory.GetGAgentAsync<ICoordinatorGAgent>(Guid.NewGuid());
        var worker1 = await GAgentFactory.GetGAgentAsync<IWorkerGAgent>(Guid.NewGuid());
        var worker2 = await GAgentFactory.GetGAgentAsync<IWorkerGAgent>(Guid.NewGuid());
        
        // Register agents for event communication
        await coordinator.RegisterAsync(worker1);
        await coordinator.RegisterAsync(worker2);
        
        return new IntegrationTestSystem
        {
            Coordinator = coordinator,
            Workers = new[] { worker1, worker2 }
        };
    }
    
    /// <summary>
    /// Seed test data into storage systems
    /// </summary>
    protected async Task SeedTestDataAsync()
    {
        var seeder = GetRequiredService<ITestDataSeeder>();
        await seeder.SeedAsync();
    }
    
    /// <summary>
    /// Wait for async operations and event propagation
    /// </summary>
    protected async Task WaitForEventPropagationAsync(int delayMs = 1000)
    {
        await Task.Delay(delayMs);
    }
}

public class IntegrationTestSystem
{
    public ICoordinatorGAgent Coordinator { get; set; }
    public IWorkerGAgent[] Workers { get; set; }
}
```

